<h1>Nate Cornell</h1>
<p>27th Ward alderman, on the Chicago ballot February 23, 2027.</p>
<p><a href="https://natecornell27.com" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign site (natecornell27.com)</a></p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>Filed nominating petitions to run for the seat held by Ald. Walter &quot;Red&quot; Burnett; on the Chicago Board of Elections candidate list as of Oct. 30, 2026. His campaign rests on affordability (no vote for a property tax increase, more housing, a Green Line station at Western and Lake, a grocery store in East Garfield Park), safety (data-driven police deployment, more detectives for violent crimes, a ward youth office), and ward services (monthly TIF transparency reports and a ward council).</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>Management consultant at Huron and then Deloitte&#39;s government practice, working on state Medicaid and public assistance programs; president of the H.O.W. United neighborhood association on the Near West Side.</p>
